* .net); just use V(tapB)/V(b2) in any .meas you add.
* SIM 12 - the full receiver: design authority, the PCB is built from this netlist (4.6 V rail since Sept 2026)
* Tests: every block and bias network together on one rail. Run .op first.
* Result: .op matches every block sim, total draw 40.5 mA / 186 mW at 4.6 V (fix round 2026-11-06: IF link + stage feeds, crystal CL 20 pF + stoppers, LNA shunt).
* Explained in fm_receiver/DESIGN_LOG.md ('Integration' and 'The supply rail') and in pcb/README.md. Old sheet notes: fm_receiver/sim_notes.md.
.model DBAS70 D(Is=85n N=1.445 Rs=29 Cjo=1.95p Vj=2.5 M=0.37 Eg=0.69 Xti=2 Bv=70 Ibv=10u)
* Cost-down 2026-11-07: BPF taps 10p/68p (0603, same 0.128 ratio, Ct 7.12p), D5 BAS70WS (DBAS70), C30 (C4_A) 1.0n, detector retrim 66.8p. Trimmer totals CT_X/CT2_X unchanged (C3 4.7p + STC3MA06, C12 6.8p + STC3MA06).
.backanno
